Subject: Competitive play: a set's players by their profile names
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The game shows its online players by their Mii names, at most 10 characters
(also what the network carries). During a set, the rows of the RANKED search
and draft screen (UpdateOnlinePlayerRow) ask the module
(src/platform/competitive_match.cpp) for its two players' profile names,
which the host gives it; any other row keeps its Mii name. FERender draws
such a name that is wider than its room (left of the row's rank) smaller, in
one row. Nothing sent over the network changes.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -77,6 +77,23 @@
 bool mscharged_competitive_leave_search(void);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// The set's players by their profile names (tweak patch 0050): the game shows
+// its online players by their Mii names (at most 10 characters, also what the
+// network carries). An online player row's name text `name` (a
+// TLTextInstance), set to the row's Mii name `mii_name` (`mii_data` its
+// RFLStoreData), and the rank text `rank` right of it: during a set, one of
+// its two players gets their profile name instead, which shows in the room
+// left of the rank; anybody else keeps the Mii name.
+void mscharged_competitive_show_name(void* name, void* rank, const unsigned short* mii_name,
+                                     const unsigned char* mii_data);
+// The front end draws text `text` (a TLTextInstance) with `matrix` (its
+// nlMatrix4): true when it shows such a profile name that is wider than its
+// room, which then draws smaller, in one row (the text's draw options to be
+// restored after the draw).
+bool mscharged_competitive_fit_text(void* text, void* matrix);
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
